Scope of application of the Act
3. (a) A court of the Maldives shall determine the death penalty upon any person, and a death penalty so determined shall be enforced in the Maldives, only in accordance with the principles and procedures set out in this Act.

(b) Notwithstanding anything to the contrary stated in any other Act, precedence shall be given to this Act in carrying out all matters relating to the determination of a death penalty and the enforcement of the penalty in the Maldives. Where a principle or procedure set out in another Act regarding the determination and enforcement of the death penalty conflicts with a principle or procedure determined in this Act, precedence shall be given to this Act.

